// Houdini Atlas — Curve Skeleton / Alien Limb starter pack
// Three VEX snippets. Each maps to one Attribute Wrangle in the node plan.
//
// === SNIPPET: vex_segment_id ===
// Wrangle name: wr_seg_id
// Run over: Points
// Purpose: freeze a stable @seg_id BEFORE any later deletion or reorder.
// Without this, "@ptnum" reorders silently and your downstream Copy to Points
// scrambles the limb.

i@seg_id = @ptnum;
// EXPECTED: spreadsheet shows @seg_id 0..63 with no gaps and no duplicates.

// === SNIPPET: vex_robust_orient ===
// Wrangle name: wr_orient
// Run over: Points
// Purpose: build a quaternion @orient per point that DOES NOT flip when
// the curve passes through a degenerate "up vector ~= tangent" region.
//
// The standard "up = (0,1,0)" trick fails when the tangent points along
// (0,1,0) or (0,-1,0) — cross(tangent, up) collapses to zero, the side
// vector is undefined, and the next segment flips 180 degrees.
//
// Fix: detect the collapse and switch to a different up axis BEFORE the
// orthonormal frame is built.

vector tangent = normalize(@N);          // resample wrote @N if "Output PointAttribs N" was on
vector up = chv("up_axis");              // expose as a Wrangle parameter (default 0,1,0)
if (length(up) < 1e-4) up = {0, 1, 0};

// Detect collapse: |t × up| close to zero ⇒ tangent is parallel to up.
vector side = cross(tangent, up);
if (length(side) < 0.05) {
    // Pick a different up axis — guaranteed non-parallel to ANY single axis.
    up = abs(tangent.y) < 0.9 ? set(0, 1, 0) : set(1, 0, 0);
    side = cross(tangent, up);
}
side = normalize(side);
vector new_up = normalize(cross(side, tangent));

// Build matrix3 then quaternion.
matrix3 m = set(side, new_up, tangent);
p@orient = quaternion(m);
v@N = tangent;
// EXPECTED: parameter-sweep "up_axis" through (0,1,0) → (0,0,1) and the limb
// must NOT flip 180° at any point along the curve.

// === SNIPPET: vex_segment_width ===
// Wrangle name: wr_width_scale
// Run over: Points
// Purpose: drive Copy to Points scale from the per-segment width.
// We do not have @width on the resampled curve directly — we re-create it
// from @curveu using a smooth taper that matches the source CSV's profile
// (1.00 at base → ~0.22 at tip).

float u = clamp(@curveu, 0.0, 1.0);
float profile = fit01(pow(1.0 - u, 1.4), 0.22, 1.0);
@pscale = profile;
// EXPECTED: capsules near the base are at full radius; capsules near the
// tip taper to roughly 22% radius.

// === HONESTY ===
// These snippets assume the resample SOP already wrote a valid @N (Output
// PointAttribs: N enabled). If @N is missing, the orient frame is undefined
// — fix the resample, do not patch around it here.
